
What is HashTable?
  - HashTable is direct implemented class of map interface.

  Syntax:
      package java.util;
     class Hashmap implements Map{
           //constructor
           //method
     }

  - It is an Legacy class and was introdused in JDK 1.0 version.
  - HashTable underline data Structure is hashtable.

HashTable Properties:
  - HashTable Contains data in key value pair and each key value pair is known as entry.
  - In HashTable, Keys Should be unique value can be duplicate.
  - HashTable can Store hetrogeneous element or different type elements at key Position.
  - We cannot store null value in hashtable.
  - HashTable does not follows the insertion and sorting order.
  - HashTable are Synchronized data structure


